  (uuid_generate_v4(), '1-25-fine-vintage-sterling-and-dark-brown-and-blue-green-boulder-turquoise-shado', '1221150105', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/1221150105/fine-vintage-turquoise-rectangle-hand?click_key=5c75ed83-faac-4cf9-9683-2746579226dc%3ALTa85c319926db56f9b1ff58315e0c89322865a564&click_sum=45d48fb3&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-89344-10-26&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&frs=1&sts=1&content_source=5c75ed83-faac-4cf9-9683-2746579226dc%253ALTa85c319926db56f9b1ff58315e0c89322865a564',
   '1.25" Fine Vintage Sterling and Dark Brown and Blue-Green Boulder Turquoise Shadowbox Earrings', 'Fine Vintage Sterling and Dark Brown and Blue-Green Boulder Turquoise Shadowbox Earrings 1.25" long x 1" wide rectangle w/o the wires. Native American Hand Stamped Arrow One weighs 9.84, the other 9.51 grams which is right about 2 nickels each, nickel=4.98 grams. These were cufflinks that I revamped into dangles using new sturdy sterling wires. Fine, gorgeous, minimal yet bold, large earrings that will definitely get noticed for their unique green-brown color and shadowbox style. The ''shadowbox'' technique consists of a cutout top layer that is usually domed and that is soldered to a solid bottom layer. It is a common jewelry technique used by Navajo and other Native American silversmiths to add interest and layering to a piece. Unsigned and unmarked they test as sterling and genuine turquoise. Being worn as cufflinks, they probably took a few bumps and knocks but have come out quite fine. One has a small scratch on the silver (see photo) near the top/side that I am quite sure I can buff out before shipping. By the style and the thickness of the silver, the fine craftsmanship and dark turquoise I would say they were most likely made in the 30''s - 40''s but I cannot guarantee this. Turquoise that has been handled a lot, worn near the skin and touched often absorbs the oils from the skin and will darken it. Since these were cufflinks, I think it shows that they were worn/handled a lot...it makes the turquoise shiny and keeps it moist (which is a good thing!).', 'turquoise-jewelry',
