   'SIGNED Vintage Native American Indian Jewelry Navajo Petit Point Sterling Silver Genuine RARE Gaspeite Bracelet Cuff Southwestern', 'Vintage Authentic Beautiful Navajo Zuni Sterling Silver Genuine RARE Gaspeite Bracelet Cuff Native American Navajo Zuni Tribe Sterling Silver Bracelet Cuff measuring 1/2”in width. The Cuff length is approximately 6 inches with gap being 1.25” total of 7.25” and is Inlaid with Beautiful genuine Gaspeite Petit Point stones. Absolutely Amazing.. and perfect for Native American jewelry collectors Stamped Sterling Hallmarked by Navajo Artist Davin Benally Matrix may vary slightly Perfect for a Gift ❤️ ~ Zuni Petit point Jewelry began around 1920-1930 and was a unique form of Turquoise Jewelry created by the Zuni Indians. A Petit Point stone is a tiny round, oval, rectangle, pear or square shaped stone hand cut by a Zuni Indian Lapidarist. Zuni Petit Point Jewelry is unique to the Zuni Indian Artisans and not made anywhere else in the world. It is special Jewelry that is impressive wearable art. Gaspeite has been found in only two locations in the world. These uncommon stones resonate strongly within the higher heart. This helps to aid forgiveness, help weight loss and may assist you to clear clutter. This is an uncommon green and brown stone that has many excellent metaphysical properties. It has been in use for hundreds of years and many of those who have used the stone have found that it has strong healing abilities.', 'turquoise-jewelry',
