  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'vintage-native-american-navajo-sterling-silver-turquoise-14k-gold-ring', '4345069241', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4345069241/vintage-native-american-navajo-sterling?click_key=5c75ed83-faac-4cf9-9683-2746579226dc%3ALTd0852972f509367daa06e478f2cad6b1688cd26a&click_sum=42fd6724&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-960714-10-5&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&pro=1&sts=1&content_source=5c75ed83-faac-4cf9-9683-2746579226dc%253ALTd0852972f509367daa06e478f2cad6b1688cd26a',
   'Vintage Native American Navajo Sterling Silver, Turquoise & 14K Gold Ring', 'Up for your consideration is a remarkable vintage Native American Navajo ring from the 1960s, crafted in sterling silver and accented with genuine 14K gold. This striking piece is artist-signed and stamped “14K” and “Sterling” on the inner band, guaranteeing both authenticity and craftsmanship. The ring showcases an impressive natural turquoise stone with a bold brown matrix and vivid aqua-blue tones, bezel-set in a custom silver mount. The top of the ring measures approximately 2 1/2 inches long by 1 inch wide, making it a substantial and eye-catching statement piece. Seven solid 14K gold beads are set at the corners and sides of the stone, adding richness and contrast to the design. Surrounding the shank and continuing throughout the band are hand-engraved silver patterns that reflect traditional Navajo motifs—each line deeply incised with precision and intention. Ring size: 10 3/4 US This is more than a ring—it''s wearable art steeped in Native American heritage, perfect for collectors or lovers of bold, historic jewelry.', 'turquoise-jewelry',
